  "summary": "The drawing uses a completely different reference-numbering scheme than the specification (e.g. the two 2x15 bus connectors are J9/J7 instead of J1/J2, the servo headers are J1/J11 instead of J3/J8, the SS54/PMEG3030EP diodes are D2/D3 instead of D1/D2, the IRLML6402/BC857/MAX3485/SPDT are Q3/Q1/U2/SW2, etc.), but per the rules component renumbering/ordering is not an anomaly. Tracing the actual nets and values, every functional relationship matches the spec: external 5V in through a Schottky (SS54, note 'forward voltage > 0.6V') to +5V; +5V to the servo rail through a low-drop Schottky (PMEG3030EP, '3A 360mV') buffered by four 100 uF caps; a 0.1 uF decoupler on the MAX3485 +3V3; the P-FET high-side battery switch gated by the SPDT through a 47k resistor onto the BAT bus pin; the BC857 auto-direction circuit (10k/5.1k divider into the base, 20k collector pull) driving the tied DE//RE of the MAX3485 with 2k/2.2k/2.2k bias on A/B; four 0-ohm selection jumpers feeding the two PWM nodes and two 0-ohm serial jumpers bridging the two servo signal pins onto the transceiver bus, each PWM node series-buffered by 1k; and the M5Unit PortB 4-pin header. The stale 'Short R10, R10 / Short R9, R11' and 'Short R13, R14 for Serial Servo' annotations are quoted verbatim in the spec as expected schematic text, not deviations. No drawing-supported behavioral anomaly was found."
}

